  "notes": "USAGE:\nA literary and somewhat old-fashioned word. In everyday conversation, Japanese speakers use キス instead. {口|くち}づけ appears mainly in novels, poetry, song lyrics, and dramatic narration. It conveys a more romantic, tender, or solemn tone than キス.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {口|くち}づけを{交|か}わす (to exchange a kiss)\n- {口|くち}づけをする (to kiss)\n- {軽|かる}い{口|くち}づけ (a light kiss)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- キス: kiss — the everyday loanword, used in casual speech\n- {接吻|せっぷん}: kiss — even more formal and literary; somewhat archaic",
